course: dictionary
lesson: 10597
title: Saying less than you mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An understatement says something smaller, weaker or less important than it really is. Often the truth is much bigger, and the listener is meant to notice the gap. «That's an understatement!» means the real thing is far bigger than the words say.
explain: In the story, the Mole's boat has just tipped him into the river, and the Rat laughs: «What's a little wet to a Water Rat?» Soaking is not a little thing, so the Rat's words make it sound tiny. He stays calm and funny, and the reader sees the bigger truth.
explain: Understatement is the opposite of hyperbole. Hyperbole makes things BIGGER: «we'll be here till we're ninety». Understatement makes them SMALLER: «bit of a wait, eh». Sarcasm is different again, because it says the opposite of what it means.
fact: An understatement makes something sound smaller than it really is.
fact: Understatement is the opposite of hyperbole, which makes things sound bigger.
fact: Understatement is often used for humour or politeness, like the Rat laughing at a soaking wet Mole.
fact: Saying «Not bad at all» about 19 out of 20 is an understatement, and it shows that Dad is proud.
exercise: «What's a little wet to a Water Rat?» Why is this an understatement? | The Rat is making the wetness sound bigger | The Rat is cross and shouting at the Mole | *The Rat makes a soaking sound much smaller than it is | The Rat is asking for a towel
exercise: Which sentence is an understatement? | «The bag weighs a thousand tonnes» | «Oh brilliant, I LOVE standing in the rain» | «We'll be here till we're ninety» | *«Bit of a wait, eh»
exercise: Dad says «Not bad at all, kiddo» about 19 out of 20. What does he really mean? | *He is proud of you | He wants you to try the test again tomorrow | He did not look at your test | He thinks the score was terrible
test: «That's an understatement!» means what? | *The truth is much bigger than the words | The truth is much smaller than the words | The words are the exact truth | The speaker is whispering
test: Which word means making something sound smaller than it really is? | Sarcasm | Shouting | Hyperbole | *Understatement
exam: Which sentence is an example of understatement? | *«Bit of a wait, eh» | «We'll be here till we're ninety» | «The bag weighs a thousand tonnes» | «Oh brilliant, I LOVE standing in the rain»
